su text "n:15199265-n | gregorian calendar | the solar calendar now in general use, introduced by Gregory XIII in 1582 to correct an error in the Julian calendar by suppressing 10 days, making Oct 5 be called Oct 15, and providing that only centenary years divisible by 400 should be leap years" ob text "{\"senseId\":\"n:15199265-n\",\"target\":\"gregorian calendar\",\"partOfSpeech\":\"n\",\"lemmas\":[\"gregorian calendar\",\"new style calendar\"],\"definition\":\"the solar calendar now in general use, introduced by Gregory XIII in 1582 to correct an error in the Julian calendar by suppressing 10 days, making Oct 5 be called Oct 15, and providing that only centenary years divisible by 400 should be leap years\",\"pyashSequence\":[\"gre2n\",\"jlet\"],\"decisionId\":\"derived-compound-0527e7b8686a75572706bb1e\"}" ya
su text "n:15199932-n | julian calendar | the solar calendar introduced in Rome in 46 b.c. by Julius Caesar and slightly modified by Augustus, establishing the 12-month year of 365 days with each 4th year having 366 days and the months having 31 or 30 days except for February" ob text "{\"senseId\":\"n:15199932-n\",\"target\":\"julian calendar\",\"partOfSpeech\":\"n\",\"lemmas\":[\"julian calendar\",\"old style calendar\"],\"definition\":\"the solar calendar introduced in Rome in 46 b.c. by Julius Caesar and slightly modified by Augustus, establishing the 12-month year of 365 days with each 4th year having 366 days and the months having 31 or 30 days except for February\",\"pyashSequence\":[\"jlun\",\"jlet\"],\"decisionId\":\"derived-compound-cb74d79a158da92481f70ccd\"}" ya
